 "_comment": "Registry of runtime state kinds (hooks/RULES.md S8): where each lives under <checkout>/.hook-only/ (or, with \"location\": \"home\", under <home>/state/<component>/: home-level state no checkout owns, written and read with root None, S1), its format, schema version, writer, whether more than one program writes it (multi_writer; then lock = the file pattern plus .lock, statefile.locked, S9) and retention (S10: until-archive, days:<settings key>, or replaced: one file every write replaces). hooks/lib/statefile.py writes only kinds listed here and refuses an object whose schema differs; hooks/tools/new-artifact.py adds entries. A registry (config/registry/): config/local.json can't override it. Keys are kind names (kebab-case), a value-as-key table. Existing state files are not listed yet: they move here category by category (debt in hooks/tests/conformance.snapshot.json).",
